#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:635
#, no-c-format
msgid "File Templates"
msgstr "Dateivörlagen"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:637
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The File Templates plugin allows you to create files based on other files."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:639
#, no-c-format
msgid "When you first install &kate;, you need to enable the plugin:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:642
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Click <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure &kate;</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:647
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the tree on the left of the screen, click <guilabel>Plugins</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:652
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In the <guilabel>Plugin Manager</guilabel> panel on the right, select "
"<guilabel>File Templates</guilabel>, and then click <guibutton>OK</"
"guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:657
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You can now use any file as a template (this creates a copy of the file with "
"an empty &URL;.) Special template files can contain macros to fill in "
"information such as your name, email address, the current date, and position "
"the cursor at a convenient position in the new file."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:662
#, no-c-format
msgid "You can easily create a new template from an open document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:663
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Templates that you save to the template folder are listed under the menu "
"item <menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>New from Template</"
"guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:666
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The template folder is part of the &kde; file system, and consists of at "
"least"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: plugins.docbook:671
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"$<envar>KDEDIR</envar>/share/applications/kate/plugins/katefiletemplates/"
"templates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: filename
#: plugins.docbook:676
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"$<envar>KDEHOME</envar>/share/applications/kate/plugins/katefiletemplates/"
"templates."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:680
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If your <envar>KDEDIRS</envar> environment variable contains additional "
"directories, those are searched for a similar subdirectory as well. If "
"equally named templates are found, the one in the local (KDEHOME) folder is "
"chosen."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:684 plugins.docbook:984 plugins.docbook:1098
#: plugins.docbook:1173 plugins.docbook:1407 plugins.docbook:1433
#: plugins.docbook:1466 plugins.docbook:1829 plugins.docbook:2102
#: plugins.docbook:2333
#, no-c-format
msgid "Menu Structure"
msgstr "Menüopbuu"

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: plugins.docbook:689
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guisubmenu>New From Template</guisubmenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Any File...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:695
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Presents you with an Open File dialog that allows you to use any file as a "
"template. If the chosen file has the extension <filename>katetemplate</"
"filename> it will be parsed for template information and macros."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: plugins.docbook:715
#, no-c-format
msgid "<guimenu>File</guimenu> <guimenuitem>New From Template</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:720
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The remainder of submenus contain links to templates. Click a menu item to "
"create a file as described by the menu item text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: menuchoice
#: plugins.docbook:729
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Manage Templates...</guimenuitem>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:731
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will launch a dialog with a list of all templates found within the "
"template directories, along with options to add, edit or remove templates."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:739
#, no-c-format
msgid "Using a &kate; Template"
msgstr "En &kate;-Vörlaag bruken"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:740
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When creating a file from a template that contains template macros, some "
"macros appear as editable variables in the text. Such variables appear as "
"underlined words in the text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:743
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The first variable will be selected, so you just have to type to edit it. If "
"the document text contains more instances of the same variable, they are "
"changed as you edit. To move to the next editable variable, press the &Tab; "
"key. When the last variable is edited, the list is dropped, and your &Tab; "
"key works as normal."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:751
#, no-c-format
msgid "Creating your own templates"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:752
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To create a new template, use the <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Manage Templates</guimenuitem></menuchoice> Item to launch the "
"template management dialog. In that, click <guibutton>New...</guibutton> to "
"launch the File Template Wizard. You will be asked for an optional file to "
"turn into a template and prompted for template information settings, and a "
"template file will be created for you."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:759
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Alternatively, you can create a template manually by adding template "
"information to the top of any file, add text and macros, and save it with "
"the <filename>katetemplate</filename> extension."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:762
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The template menu is automatically updated if you chose to store your "
"template in the template directory."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:767
#, no-c-format
msgid "Editing templates"
msgstr "Bewerken vun Vörlagen"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:768
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To edit a template, use the <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu> "
"<guimenuitem>Manage Templates...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>. Select the "
"template you want to work on and click <guibutton>Edit...</guibutton>, and "
"the template file will be opened. Close the dialog, edit the template file "
"as desired, save it and close it. Changes to templates take immediate "
"effect; you can activate the template to test your changes after saving it."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:779
#, no-c-format
msgid "The &kate; Template Format"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:780
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"If you use files with the extension <filename>katetemplate</filename>, they "
"will be parsed for template information, macros and a cursor position."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:785
#, no-c-format
msgid "Template information"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:786
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While reading in the file, the parser keeps lines beginning with the phrase "
"<constant>katetemplate:</constant> and searches them for template "
"information in the form VARIABLENAME=VALUE. The first line not starting with "
"<constant>katetemplate:</constant> will be taken as the start of the "
"template contents. VALUE may contain any character but equal sign (=). Legal "
"variable names are:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: plugins.docbook:795
#, no-c-format
msgid "Template"
msgstr "Vörlaag"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:796
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the template name, displayed in the <menuchoice><guimenu>File</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>New from Template</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: plugins.docbook:801
#, no-c-format
msgid "Group"
msgstr "Koppel"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:802
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The group places the template in a submenu of the <menuchoice><guimenu>File</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>New from Template</guimenuitem></menuchoice> menu."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: plugins.docbook:806
#, no-c-format
msgid "Name"
msgstr "Naam"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:807
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This is the name that will be set for the document, and displayed in the "
"file list and title bar. If the name contains <userinput>%N</userinput> that "
"will be replaced with a number, incrementing if more documents have the same "
"name."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: plugins.docbook:814
#, no-c-format
msgid "Highlight"
msgstr "Rutheven"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:815
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The plugin will try to set the Highlight for the new document to the value "
"of this variable. The value should be the name, as found in "
"<menuchoice><guimenu>Tools</guimenu> <guimenuitem>Highlighting</guimenuitem> "
"</menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: varname
#: plugins.docbook:824
#, no-c-format
msgid "Description"
msgstr "Beschrieven"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:825
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A short informative description of the template. This is currently used to "
"set a <guimenuitem>What's this?</guimenuitem> string for the menu item, but "
"may be used for additional purposes in the future."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:830
#, no-c-format
msgid "Author"
msgstr "Autor"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:831
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A string identifying the author, for example in the form <userinput>Name &lt;"
"email address&gt;</userinput>. This is currently used to set a "
"<guimenuitem>What's this?</guimenuitem> string for the menu item, but may be "
"used for additional purposes in the future."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:843
#, no-c-format
msgid "Template Macros"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:845
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"While parsing the template contents, macros in the form <userinput>%{NAME}</"
"userinput> or <userinput>${NAME}</userinput> are expanded. If you use the "
"<userinput>$</userinput> prefix, the expanded macro will be treated as a "
"editable variable when a document is created from the template, whereas if "
"you use <userinput>%</userinput> it is not, unless expanding failed."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:851
#, no-c-format
msgid "The following macros are expanded:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literal
#: plugins.docbook:853
#, no-c-format
msgid "time"
msgstr "Tiet"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:854
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expands to the current time in your locale format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literal
#: plugins.docbook:858
#, no-c-format
msgid "date"
msgstr "Datum"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:859
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expands to the current date in short format."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literal
#: plugins.docbook:863
#, no-c-format
msgid "datetime"
msgstr "Datum un Tiet"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:864
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Expands to the current date and time, formatted as a string according to "
"your locale."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literal
#: plugins.docbook:869
#, no-c-format
msgid "year"
msgstr "Johr"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:870
#, no-c-format
msgid "The current year as a four digit number."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literal
#: plugins.docbook:874
#, no-c-format
msgid "month"
msgstr "Maand"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:875
#, no-c-format
msgid "The full name of the current month, according to your locale."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literal
#: plugins.docbook:878
#, no-c-format
msgid "<literal>day</literal>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:879
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expands to the current day of the month."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literal
#: plugins.docbook:882
#, no-c-format
msgid "hostname"
msgstr "Reeknernaam"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:883
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expands to the hostname of your computer."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literal
#: plugins.docbook:886
#, no-c-format
msgid "index"
msgstr "Index"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:887
#, no-c-format
msgid "Expands to 'i'."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literal
#: plugins.docbook:889
#, no-c-format
msgid "fullname"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:890
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Expands to your full name, as defined in the owner addressee in your "
"standard &kde; addressbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literal
#: plugins.docbook:894
#, no-c-format
msgid "firstname"
msgstr "Vörnaam"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:895
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Expands to your first name, as defined in the owner addressee in your "
"standard &kde; addressbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: literal
#: plugins.docbook:899
#, no-c-format
msgid "lastname"
msgstr "Familiennaam"

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:900
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Expands to your last name, as defined in the owner addressee in your "
"standard &kde; addressbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: term
#: plugins.docbook:909
#, no-c-format
msgid "email"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:910
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Expands to your email address, as defined in the owner address in your "
"standard &kde; addressbook."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:922
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Any macro not in the above list is treated as an editable variable no matter "
"the prefix. If the same variable occurs multiple times in the template, they "
"can be edited at once after creating a document from the template."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: plugins.docbook:929
#, no-c-format
msgid "Setting the cursor position"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: plugins.docbook:930
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The special macro <userinput>${cursor}</userinput> will be replaced with a "
"vertical bar and added to the end of the list of editable variables, "
"independent of its location in the text."
msgstr ""

